# Ignore dependencies, generated output, local runtime state, device diagnostics,
# and exported teaching data. Keep source, dependency lockfiles, shared Xcode
# configuration, design artwork, documented environment examples and test fixtures.
# Scope captures and temporary workspaces by path so source assets stay visible.
# Ignoring a path does not delete local data or untrack an existing Git file.
# Inspect a rule with: git check-ignore -v --no-index -- path/to/file

# JavaScript dependencies and package-manager caches
node_modules/
.npm-cache/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/cache/
.yarn/unplugged/
.yarn/install-state.gz
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache

# Build output and frontend tool caches
# build_local.sh writes dist/ and build/local/; the native entry points use
# ipad/build/{device,simulator}/, iphone/build/{device,simulator}/ and vision/build/{device,simulator}/.
# The build/ rule also covers deploy_ipad.sh's ipad/build/deploy-device/ logs,
# device/signing reports, products, and native UI verification attachments.
# Camera/joint collaboration checks use build/{screen-validation,ipad-screen-test}/
# and ipad/build/screen-tests/, including captured frames and Xcode results.
# Pose capture and viewport gesture checks use build/screen-{capture,viewport}-validation/;
# peer.json, state.json, command.json, saved poses and native captures stay local.
# Menu review captures and preview bundles use build/{menu-review,menu-validation}/.
# Teaching popup checks and typography reviews use build/teaching-pose-popup-validation/
# and build/teaching-tree-type-review/, including browser captures and local runners.
# Independent-browser collaboration and iPad top-action checks use
# build/{ipad-remote-collaboration,ipad-collaboration-top-actions}/; pairing
# credentials, exported projects, native test plans and screenshots stay local.
# Windows USB companion checks use build/ipad-windows-usb/ for the downloadable
# helper bundle, extracted package checks, browser captures and native test results.
# Adjustable joint-limit checks use build/robot-soft-limits/ for menu captures,
# collaboration credentials and simulated device command/state files.
# Coupled-wrist UI checks use build/robot-joint-coupling/ for browser captures.
# Mac/iPad realtime checks use build/ipad-realtime-*/ and ipad/build/realtime-testing/;
# performance samples, device/signing settings, captures and Python environments stay local.
# Bidirectional USB invitation checks use build/ipad-screen-invitations/ for
# browser/native captures, readiness markers, device reports and deployment logs.
# The persistent web service uses build/service/.
# Surface-polyline UI artifacts (selection/new drafts, constraint/help dialogs,
# tool/pose editing, undo, planning, progress/replay and start-pose ghosts),
# imported-project reproductions, solver A/B source snapshots, serialized robot
# collision hulls, playback verification and service-index backups belong in
# test-artifacts/polyline-*/; maintained regression runners stay in tests/.
# Reset-confirmation backup checks keep screenshots and service-index backups
# in test-artifacts/global-reset-export/; exported ZIPs use temporary workspaces.
# Shared-preset migration and map-origin navigation checks use
# test-artifacts/{shared-robot-presets,map-origin-navigation}/ for browser
# captures and service-index backups; their regression runners stay in tests/.
dist/
build/
out/
output/
.vite/
.vite-temp/
*.tsbuildinfo
vite.config.*.timestamp-*

# Node.js and browser diagnostic dumps
*.heapsnapshot
*.cpuprofile
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
/core
/core.*
*.dmp

